# Raw genealogy data must never be committed, even to a private repo.
# A GEDCOM contains full names, birthdates, and birthplaces for LIVING people.
# The published site is a generated derivative behind an access code; these are
# the raw sources and they stay on your own machine.
*.ged
*.gedcom
*.GED
*.ftm
*.gramps
*.gpkg
/raw/
/private/

# Scans and family photos - keep the originals off the repo, they are large
# and often contain document images with sensitive detail.
/originals/

# Bulk media belongs in R2, served through the gated Worker - not in the repo.
# Cloudflare Pages caps files at 25 MiB and does not fetch Git LFS objects, so
# LFS-tracked images deploy as pointer files and every photo renders broken.
/media/
/scans/
*.lfs

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
